# /etc/pivtab: dm-piv views opened by the initramfs (packaging/README.md).
# Research prototype without external cryptographic review.
#
# NAME        DEVICE                      LUKS-KEY   HIDDEN-SECRET  OPTIONS
# NAME          mapping name (piv-...); views appear as /dev/mapper/NAME-decoy
#               and /dev/mapper/NAME-hidden.
# DEVICE        block device or partition holding the LUKS2 volume; prefer a
#               stable path such as /dev/disk/by-partuuid/... or by-id/....
# LUKS-KEY      stock LUKS passphrase/key file, or "ask" (prompt at boot).
# HIDDEN-SECRET hidden key file (32 bytes), or "ask" (prompt for a hidden
#               passphrase at boot; needs the hidden-passphrase option).
# OPTIONS       comma-separated, or "-":
#   embed-keys        copy the key files into the initramfs. Anyone who can
#                     read the initramfs (usually unencrypted in /boot) then
#                     has both keys and can prove the hidden volume exists.
#   hidden-passphrase HIDDEN-SECRET is a passphrase (Argon2id), not a key.
#   kdf-cost=N        Argon2id cost tier 1-4 of that passphrase (default 3).
#
# Key file paths are allowed only with embed-keys: nothing else makes them
# available at boot. This file itself (copied into the initramfs) reveals that a
# hidden volume is configured.
#
# piv-native  /dev/disk/by-partuuid/0000  ask        ask            hidden-passphrase
